The bubble-player part of the voice-messages epic (#120), squashed from
the incremental patch series. The two-layer playback architecture stays
intact: each bubble renders a force-muted <audio> whose events are
mirrored to the global singleton in MediaPlayerMutexContext (which
produces the sound and drives auto-advance). The custom controls only
drive the LOCAL muted element; the existing mirroring does the rest, so
real `ended` events keep firing on the singleton.

Controls (setting experimentalAudioPlayerControls, default ON — see
"defaults" below): play/pause, seek bar, m:ss elapsed/total, and a pill
cycling 1x/1.5x/2x. The rate is global (MediaPlayerMutexContext
playbackRate + setPlaybackRate); setPlaybackRate also sets
defaultPlaybackRate on both elements because loading a new src resets
playbackRate to defaultPlaybackRate (HTML media load algorithm), so the
chosen rate survives track changes / auto-advance. One stable render
tree: toggling the setting mid-playback must not remount the local
<audio> at 0 (controls={!customControlsEnabled}, never a different tree).
Two-row layout: right of the play button the waveform takes the full
width, a meta row below carries time (start) and the speed pill (end).
Narrow viewports: bubbles claim min(70vw, 340px) — 78vw pushed the
outgoing bubble's pill past the screen edge, shrink-to-content made the
waveform too cramped to seek by touch.

Waveform (progressive enhancement — playback NEVER waits on it, any
failure silently keeps the plain range): peaks.ts getPeaks(src) =
in-session bounded promise cache (~100 FIFO, keyed by the FRAGMENT-LESS
URL, see identity below; no persistent cache — measure first, User
Timing sc:waveform:* feeds the web-app Diagnostics "Waveform (ms)"
section) -> fetch -> decodeAudioData on the main thread (a plain worker
cannot construct an AudioContext, only the max-abs bucketing is
offloaded) -> shared module worker, resolved relative to the document
(new URL('waveform-worker.js', location.href)) so subpath deploys don't
404. ~4s budget via Promise.race + fetch abort; a worker load error
(async!) flips to a permanent null fallback and settles all pending
callers — no hang, no leaked AudioBuffers. The canvas renders UNDER the
range input, which stays THE interaction layer (drag guard, keyboard via
a Message.tsx keydown carve-out, aria) but goes fully transparent;
appearance:none collapses the input's intrinsic height, so the wrap
reserves 32px explicitly (also prevents the bubble-geometry jump when
peaks arrive).

Remembered position (positionStore.ts): localStorage map keyed by src,
value {t, at}, capped ~300 oldest-pruned, every storage access
try/caught, blob: srcs skipped (ephemeral recorder previews). Restore
only into a fresh element (currentTime < 1) and only to t in
(1, duration-1); save throttled ~2s while playing + on pause; cleared by
the SINGLETON's natural `ended` (fires across bubble unmount). The mutex
takeover cleanup saves the exact position BEFORE zeroing (the queued
pause event would otherwise see 0) — but near-end counts as ended: on a
natural end the local element can lag the singleton's `ended` by tens of
ms, and saving duration-ε would resurrect the entry the singleton just
cleared and make the next play end/auto-advance instantly. In custom
mode a deactivated bubble KEEPS its shown position (display matches what
replay will do); native mode zeroes like upstream.

Singleton/bubble sync invariants (each direction fixed a real bug —
KEEP ALL FOUR when resolving conflicts here):
- local -> singleton on play: a restored/scrubbed local currentTime is
  carried onto a singleton that just started this src fresh (it
  otherwise starts at 0). One-way; only when singleton < 1s progress.
- singleton -> local on remount: a bubble (re)mounting while its message
  plays adopts the singleton's currentTime (>1s progress, local fresh
  <1s) — fixes 0:00-counting-up-while-sound-is-midway on profile/chat
  switch (upstream #6378). Ungated: also fixes the native display.
- singleton 'seeked' -> local, delta-guarded (>0.5s): mini-player /
  media-session seeks must reach the bubble or its display desyncs and
  the two positionStore writers fight; the delta guard prevents
  ping-pong with the local->global onSeeking mirror.
- restore never yanks back a singleton mid-playing the same src (>= 1s
  progress skips), so auto-advance onto a half-heard message restores
  but a remounting bubble can't rewind live playback.

Per-message identity: a forwarded voice message shares the original's
content-deduped blob -> identical URL -> both bubbles mirrored as
playing and one shared resume position (pre-existing upstream, glaring
with custom controls). All three src call sites (bubble, gallery,
auto-advance in NextVoiceMessagePlayerContext) append an inert
'#msg=<id>' fragment — NOT a media fragment, never sent to the server —
making mirroring, mutex identity and the position store per-message,
while getPeaks strips the fragment so original + forward still decode
once per blob. If you touch a src construction, keep the fragment at
ALL sites or mirroring silently stops matching.

Auto-advance (NextVoiceMessagePlayerContext): ended-driven advance and
playNext() share one advanceOrStop() path; the sequential-playback
staleness guard runs BEFORE the stop branch so a stale parked ended
event can't stop an unrelated message.

Defaults: flipped to on after four phases of polish; the switch stays in
Settings -> Experimental features for the native controls. No migration
needed and none shipped: the browser runtime persists only keys a user
touched, so a stored `false` can only mean a deliberate opt-out — which
is exactly what the fork's voice_player_disabled startup event counts.

Pure helpers (formatAudioTime, nextPlaybackRate, drawBars) are
unit-tested; positionStore via injectable storage + clock. The
audioPlayer mocha suite lands with the global-player commit (it also
covers voicePlayerSurface from there).
